# Hey there! 👋

I'm a Robotics Engineering student who loves building things that move, think, and (hopefully) don't break on the first run.

I spend most of my time somewhere between CAD models and microcontroller datasheets. Whether it's designing a mechanism in SolidWorks or debugging serial communication at 2 AM — I genuinely enjoy the entire process of bringing a robot from idea to reality.

---

## 🔧 What I Work With

**Languages:** C++ · Embedded C · Python · HTML  
**Tools & Platforms:** Arduino · SolidWorks · OpenCV  
**Domains:** Robotics · Embedded Systems · Computer Vision

I wouldn't say I'm an expert in all of these, but I've used each of them enough to build real, working projects — and that's what matters to me.

---

## 🚀 Projects

### Live Monitoring Robotic Rover
This was a college group project where we built a rover that could be monitored and controlled in real-time. We handled everything from the mechanical chassis design to the software stack for live video feed and sensor data. It was my first big team project, and honestly, coordinating with a group taught me just as much as the technical side did.

### 6 DOF Robotic Arm
This one is close to my heart — entirely self-funded and built solo from scratch. A 6 Degree of Freedom robotic arm that I designed, fabricated, and programmed myself. From the kinematic calculations to the 3D printed parts to writing the control firmware — every bit of it was a learning experience. Probably the project I'm most proud of so far.

